// Ling language — LALRPOP grammar skeleton
//
// This file defines the grammar for the Ling programming language using the
// LALRPOP parser-generator.  It is kept here as the canonical grammar
// reference; the hand-written recursive-descent parser in
// `src/parser/mod.rs` is used by the current interpreter and must stay in
// sync with the rules below.
//
// To regenerate the parser: ensure `lalrpop` is listed in
// `[build-dependencies]` and call `lalrpop::process_root()` from build.rs.
//
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Token aliases  (produced by src/lexer/mod.rs)
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
//   Bind  Do  Fn  Mod  Type
//   If  Else  While  For  In  Match  Return
//   Own  Lend  Share  Move  Copy  Async  Wait
//   Ok  Bad  None  As  Where
//   Ident(String)  Number(String)  String(String)  Bool(bool)
//   Plus  Minus  Star  Slash  Percent
//   Eq  EqEq  Ne  Lt  Gt  Le  Ge  And  Or  Not
//   Arrow  FatArrow  Dot  DotDot  Ampersand  ColonColon
//   LParen  RParen  LBrace  RBrace  LBracket  RBracket
//   Comma  Colon  Semicolon

// NOTE: lalrpop requires an `extern { }` block mapping token types, plus
// full grammar rules.  The complete implementation is left for a future
// milestone; the hand-written parser is authoritative in the meantime.
//
// Minimal stub so lalrpop does not choke on this file:

grammar;

